# Modelfile.smart.registry -- portable fallback source for sim-smart
# (MODEL_SMART)
#
# Modelfile.smart's `FROM` line points at an absolute path on the original
# author's machine (a GGUF cached there by a now-retired LM Studio install).
# That path does not exist on any other machine, so `ollama create sim-smart
# -f ollama/Modelfile.smart` fails everywhere else. This file is the portable
# fallback: `FROM qwen3.5:9b` pulls the same model family from the Ollama
# registry instead of a local file (verified reachable: `qwen3.5:9b` returns
# HTTP 200 from https://registry.ollama.ai/v2/library/qwen3.5/manifests/9b).
#
# `ollama/Modelfile.smart` (the local GGUF) remains the PREFERRED source on
# the author's machine -- it avoids a ~5.2 GB registry download and was
# already verified to import cleanly. `scripts/ollama_setup.py` only falls
# back to this file when the local GGUF path from Modelfile.smart is not
# present on disk (see that script's smart-model source selection).
#
# PARAMETER lines copied verbatim from ollama/Modelfile.smart -- keep the two
# files' PARAMETER blocks in sync if either changes.

FROM qwen3.5:9b

PARAMETER num_ctx 20480
PARAMETER temperature 0.4
PARAMETER top_p 0.8
PARAMETER top_k 20
PARAMETER min_p 0
